# Smoky Lounge's "At the beginning of your first main phase, add {R}{R}. Spend this mana only to cast Room spells and unlock
# doors" (CR 106.6, 709.5e). Bot1 casts it as Smoky Lounge on turn 1 with Black Lotus's {R}{R}{R}, and on turn 3 the {R}{R}
# arrive in the pool. They cannot cast Mind Stone, a nonRoom spell, though it costs only {2} (with nothing else untapped
# the cast is refused), nor pay Mind Stone's "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card" (an ability); Mind Stone is
# cast with Mox Sapphires' {U}{U} instead (`Spend: U, U`). The {R}{R} then pay, with a {U} and Mind Stone's {C}, for unlocking
# Misty Salon's door ({3}{U}), a special action that is neither a spell nor an ability. "When you unlock this door" makes
# an X/X blue flying Spirit, X being the unlocked doors among Rooms Bot1 controls as it resolves: this Room's two,
# the door just unlocked counted with the one from before (CR 709.5c): a 2/2.

